Fixed and committed as `93b9557`. The old cropped-wheel animation no longer plays on Sign up — not on the first hover, not ever.

## What was happening

`enterUp` fell back to `fx.signUpHover(true)` whenever the clip wasn't decoded yet, and that ran the v1 reaction: the 55° spin of the cropped wheel copy plus the gold door-seam glow. The frames take ~3 s to decode after the entrance, so the first hover almost always landed in that window and showed the old animation; by the second hover the clip was ready.

## What changed

- [HeroVault.tsx](src/components/HeroVault.tsx): the wheel spin and seam glow are now gated on `!FX.wheelClip` instead of "clip not currently showing", so with the clip enabled they never run — at any load state, and on click too (the 360° spin and seam pulse are gone as well). Hinge glint, arrow slide and button lift are untouched.
- [HeroButtons.tsx](src/components/HeroButtons.tsx): tracks whether the pointer/focus/tap is on Sign up, and starts the clip the moment its load finishes if you're still hovering — no second hover needed.
- [clipPlayer.ts](src/lib/clipPlayer.ts): warning text updated ("Sign up keeps the static vault"), since it no longer claims a v1 fallback.

## Verified

Fresh page, hover at ~2.6 s (clip still loading):

| moment | wheel transform | seam | clip |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| idle | `matrix(1,0,0,1,…)` | `rgba(226,184,103,0)` | unpainted, opacity 0 |
| hover +300 ms | unchanged | transparent | 0 |
| hover +900 ms | unchanged | transparent | 0 |
| hover +1800 ms | unchanged | transparent | painted, opacity 1 — started on its own while still hovering |
| after leaving | unchanged | transparent | cleared, wheel copy visible again |
| second hover | unchanged | transparent | painted, opacity 1 |

No rotation at any point. Frames renamed away: still no spin, seam stays transparent, exactly one console warning. `FX.wheelClip = false`: v1 comes back exactly (wheel at 55°, seam `rgba(226,184,103,0.55)`, zero clip requests). `tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` clean. The dev server is still live on `127.0.0.1:5173`.

One residual: the first hover still has a short gap before the clip starts, because the frames only begin loading after the entrance (2.618 s) and take ~3 s to decode. It's now a pause with the hinge glint, not the old animation — starting the decode earlier would close it.
