Fixed — commit `aa6442a`. The first hover now starts in roughly the same time as every later one.

## What was wrong

`load()` decoded all 81 frames before resolving, so `ready()` stayed false for ~3 s after the entrance. Until then every hover fell through to "clip not loaded", and the first hover that landed in that window only started once the whole set had decoded. Later hovers were instant because the array was complete.

## What changed

- [clipPlayer.ts](src/lib/clipPlayer.ts): frames now stream. The first batch of 10 is decoded before `load()` resolves, so the clip is playable in a few hundred milliseconds; the remaining batches fill in behind playback, each one yielding to `requestIdleCallback` before it runs. A frame that hasn't arrived yet holds the previous one instead of aborting the draw, and `last()` is driven by the URL count, so playback still targets frame 81.
- [HeroButtons.tsx](src/components/HeroButtons.tsx): decoding starts 200 ms after mount via an idle callback with a 400 ms timeout, instead of 2.618 s after the entrance. The timeout matters — without it the entrance's rAF work starved the idle callback and loading began only after the animation finished.

## Measured

Time from hover to the first painted clip frame, first hover vs second on a fresh page (includes Playwright dispatch and 25 ms polling, so the real figure is lower):

| hover at | first | second |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0.6 s | 261 ms | 278 ms |
| 0.8 s | 249 ms | 184 ms |
| 1.5 s | 275 ms | 192 ms |

Before the change the same first hover painted at ~1.8 s and was still blank at 1.5 s. The first/second gap is now within the harness's own noise.

Correctness alongside it:

- **Every frame still plays** — the held frame after a full run hashes identically (`78025308`) whether the clip was hovered at 1 s (streaming) or 8 s (fully decoded).
- **Entrance unharmed** — chips fade 0→1 in 2128 ms both with the prefetch and with `FX.wheelClip = false` (no prefetch at all), with zero long tasks recorded.
- **CLS 0.00** in both runs.
- **Frames missing** — no clip, seam transparent, exactly one console warning, and the click still navigates (1.22 s). No old wheel animation exists to fall back to any more.

The one case that's still not instant: hovering within the first ~400 ms of page load, while the first batch is decoding. Everything after that is immediate.
