Removed — commit `73114bd`. The text no longer fades or slides away on scroll, and it can't be made unclickable by scrolling either.

## What was doing it

`hero-timeline.ts` still had the scroll handoff from when a pinned sequence lived below the hero. On every scroll event it wrote `copy.style.opacity = 1 - scrollY/(6% of viewport)`, translated the column up by 21 px, and at 98 % of that ramp set `pointer-events: none` on it. With the hero now being the whole page, that meant the only text on the site vanished ~55 px into any scroll.

Deleted: the whole `onScroll` handler, the `scroll` listener, and the `parallaxOn` bookkeeping that re-armed parallax at the top.

The headline's pointer drift survives — it used to work only through those scroll-time inline styles, so it now writes its transform directly in the parallax loop (same 8 px, same 0.08 lerp). Vault rotation is untouched. On mobile it was already off (`parallax` is desktop-only).

![Hero at 375 after scrolling](docs/hero-shots/mobile-scrolled.jpg)

## Verified

| | 1440×900 | 375×800 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| copy opacity at scroll 0 | 1 | 1 |
| copy opacity at max scroll | 1 (page doesn't scroll) | **1** at scrollY 441 (was 0) |
| copy `pointer-events` | auto | **auto** (was `none`) |
| CTA at that scroll | hit-tests to the copy | visible, hit-tests to the copy; two taps → `/signin` |
| parallax | `matrix(1,0,0,1,7.89,-7.82)` after a pointer move — still drifting | n/a (desktop only) |
| console errors | none | none |

`tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` are clean.

Worth noting: this also clears the mobile blocker I reported two turns ago — the Sign in / Sign up buttons were being made untappable by that same handoff once a phone user scrolled down to them. They now work after scrolling, verified by tapping through to `/signin`.
