**1. `index.html` has no viewport meta — the phone layout will not trigger on a real device.** The document lays out at ~980 CSS px, so `(max-width: 767px)` never matches and phones keep the desktop layout site-wide. This predates the work and is outside the allowed files, so I changed nothing. The fix is one line: `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">`. Until that lands, everything above only exists at genuine 360–430px widths.

**2. The keypad clip is desktop-only in code.** `padViewport()` in [HeroButtons.tsx](src/components/HeroButtons.tsx#L33-L36) refuses to build the keypad player below 768px ("no phone-sized keypad frame set"), so tapping Sign in on a phone uses the flat v2 keys instead. That's why the keypad row above was measured by building the player at 900px and resizing to 360/390 — the rect it *would* use is correct, but phones never get the clip. Relaxing that gate is a one-line change in a file outside my scope; say the word and I'll make it.

One interpretation to confirm: "0.8 × zone height / vaultHeightFraction × vaultAspect" is dimensionally ambiguous, so I read it as *vault body height = 80% of the zone height, width following the frame aspect*, then capped at 61.8% of viewport width — the resolved widths in the table above are what that produces.
