The keypad now plays itself back down before the wheel starts — no more instant cut.

## The new sequence

| t | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| 3.3s | keypad clip fades in, keys light one after another |
| 5.5s | fully lit (frame 48 of 96) |
| 5.5 → 6.4s | keys hold lit |
| 6.4 → 8.2s | **reverse**: frames step back down at the clip's own 24fps, staying fully opaque the whole way |
| 8.4s | wheel fades in and turns once |
| 11.7 → 15.2s | wheel closes, vault back at rest (~15.6s total) |

I proved the reverse is a real reverse rather than a fade by hashing the keypad canvas every 150ms: the pixels change continuously from 6.4s to 8.2s while opacity sits at `1.00`, and only then does the fade-out begin — the wheel doesn't touch the screen until 8.4s.

![Keypad fully lit, before the reverse](docs/hero-shots/intro/_preview/01-keypad-lit.png)

## And the reason you saw nothing at all

Your browser's console had this on every load: `[fx] wheel clip unavailable — Sign up keeps the static vault`. That's a genuine bug in [clipPlayer.ts](src/lib/clipPlayer.ts#L270):

- The 4-second load budget was measured on the wall clock.
- Browsers **defer image decoding while a page is in the background**, and your preview panel loads in the background (it reports `document.hidden === true` while the chat has focus).
- So the decode sat there for seconds past the budget, the loader threw, and the wheel clip was discarded permanently — even after the panel became visible.

The budget now counts only time the page is awake, so a clip that starts loading in an unfocused tab survives until it's on screen. Verified by forcing a 5-second stall inside a hidden tab: previously that ends in the warning and no clip, now it loads with zero warnings and plays on reveal. Your tab's console is now clean on both clips.

Files touched: [HeroButtons.tsx](src/components/HeroButtons.tsx) (the sequence, with the reverse phase) and [clipPlayer.ts](src/lib/clipPlayer.ts#L253) (awake-time budget). I also dropped the temporary `seek` helper I'd added last round — the reverse returns the keypad to frame 0 on its own, so the first Sign in hover still cascades in from a dark keypad.

## Re-verified after both changes

| Check | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Keypad reverse visible | frames change 6.4s → 8.2s at opacity 1.00 |
| Wheel starts after the reverse finishes | 8.4s, not before |
| Hover after the intro | Sign up wheel 1.00 → 0.00; Sign in keypad 1.00 → 0.00 |
| Second visit / reduced motion | no clips, no flag written |
| `?intro=1` replay | plays regardless of the stored flag |
| Slow decode in a hidden tab | no `unavailable` warning, plays on reveal |
| `tsc --noEmit`, `npm run build` | pass |

