Here it is on an iPhone 18 Pro Max — but first, the important part: it wasn't showing the phone layout at all until I fixed one line.

## The phone was getting the desktop layout

Before this, `index.html` had no viewport meta, so Mobile Safari laid the page out at **980 CSS px** and scaled it down — the mobile rules never matched. The first capture at 440×956 reported `viewport: 980x2130`, a 1320px-tall stage and a single-line headline. I added `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">` to [index.html](index.html#L4); the same capture now reports `440x956`, stage 365px, and the real phone composition.

![iPhone 18 Pro Max, first screen](docs/hero-shots/iphone-18-pro-max/_preview/01-first-screen.png)

| Element | Top | Note |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Vault zone | 0 → 365 | 38.2svh, body 61.8% of width |
| Eyebrow | 386 | 21px inset |
| H1 | 418 → 516 | 42px, two lines |
| Sign up | 537 → 592 | **56.2% of screen height** |
| Sign in | 613 → 668 | ends at 69.9% |
| Sandbox note | 681 | |
| Body | 734 → 889 | 16px/1.618 |
| Chips | 923 → 955 | one scrolling row |

No horizontal overflow (`scrollWidth 440`), and the whole hero — vault, headline, both buttons, paragraph and chip row — sits inside one 956px screen.

The intro runs here too, wheel-only:

![iPhone 18 Pro Max, intro wheel turning](docs/hero-shots/iphone-18-pro-max/_preview/04-intro-wheel.png)

![iPhone 18 Pro Max, chip row scrolled](docs/hero-shots/iphone-18-pro-max/_preview/03-chips-scrolled.png)

## Two things this size exposes

**The chips land exactly at the fold.** Content is 976px tall against a 956px screen, so the row's bottom edge sits 1px above the cut and reads as clipped in the shots. On the actual device the home-indicator area overlaps that last 34px. If you want the row fully clear I'd trim ~24px from the vault zone at this height — say so and I'll do it.

**No keypad on the phone.** The keypad clip is still gated to ≥768px (`padViewport()`), so the intro here is the wheel alone. That gate is the one thing standing between iPhone and the full keypad-runs-back-down sequence.

Full-resolution captures (1320×2868, DPR 3) are in [docs/hero-shots/iphone-18-pro-max](docs/hero-shots/iphone-18-pro-max): [01-first-screen.png](docs/hero-shots/iphone-18-pro-max/01-first-screen.png), [04-intro-wheel.png](docs/hero-shots/iphone-18-pro-max/04-intro-wheel.png), [03-chips-scrolled.png](docs/hero-shots/iphone-18-pro-max/03-chips-scrolled.png). The capture harness is [iphone-shots.mjs](scripts/iphone-shots.mjs).

The viewport meta is now uncommitted alongside the intro work — `index.html`, `HeroButtons.tsx` and `clipPlayer.ts`.
