a3c29c7 feat(signup): add the role stepper component and its copy
b270126 fix(vault): fade the canvas from the drawn edge, not the canvas edge
```

Three commits for four slices: the band fix is its own, and slices 2 + 3 share one component and one stylesheet, so the stepper landed as one commit and the card/markup as the next. Every commit builds.

## The pale band — cause and fix

The signup anchor shifts the whole stage **14.6vw** right (`--vault-x` 61.8 → 76.4), so the canvas begins at 210px on 1440 and the photo's own left cut falls **inside** the old 12% mask at ~69% opacity — a hard vertical step there, not at the canvas edge.

| | largest column step, left third |
| --- | --- |
| 1440 before | **−5.06 / 255 at x 245** (the drawn edge) |
| 1440 after | none at 245 (residual 3.2 at x 71, the gradient's own texture) |
| 1920 before | **−14.39 at x 443** |
| 1920 after | −1.35 at x 473 (inside the new ramp) |

![before](docs/hero-shots/signup/polish/band-before-crop.jpg)
![after](docs/hero-shots/signup/polish/band-after-crop.jpg)

The paint pass now writes the drawn rect's left edge to `--draw-left`, and `.hero-canvas` runs a **144px** mask fade from it. That is the one place I left the "signup files only" fence: the mask lives on the hero canvas, so [hero.css](src/styles/hero.css) and one line of [HeroVault.tsx](src/components/HeroVault.tsx) had to change. No position, clip or token moved.

**The bottom strips are not reproducible here**: `document.scrollHeight` equals the viewport exactly at 1280/1440/1920 and the row means run 219 → 227 monotonically to the last pixel. That points at `min-height: 100svh` ending above the window's visual bottom (browser chrome), leaving the body's `#eff1f0` visible — a lighter strip under the `#e1e7e8` gradient. The fix lives outside my allowed files (`body` background or `100lvh` on the layout); tell me and I'll do it.

