Fixed. The buttons weren't in the signup card — they were the hero's CTA row and headline, left invisible by the way back from `/signup`.

## What was happening

Coming home runs a "copy returns from the left" tween. That tween was created with `delay: 0.382` and killed by the effect's own cleanup, so the copy froze in its **exit pose**: `translate(-89px)` plus `opacity: 0`. Measured 6s after the return, before the fix:

```
.hero-h1        opacity 0   transform: translate(-89px, 0px)   ← headline
.hero-cta-block opacity 0   transform: translate(-89px, 0px)   ← both CTA buttons
.hero-body      opacity 1   transform: translate(-89px, 0px)   ← permanently shifted 89px
.hero-chips     opacity 1   transform: translate(-89px, 0px)
```

So the headline and the buttons were present, sized 427×317 and 127×55, and simply not painted. Nothing to do with the stepper, which is why clicking through the roles looked fine right up until you left the card.

## Three fixes

**[Hero.tsx](src/components/Hero.tsx)** — the reveal now starts from a cleared timer instead of a tween `delay`, and the teardown always lands the copy at rest (`x/y 0`, `opacity 1`, transform cleared) instead of leaving it wherever a killed tween stopped. A reveal that is interrupted can no longer hide anything.

**[Signup.tsx](src/pages/Signup.tsx)** — "Change role" (and any step click) that landed during the 0.764s slide was silently dropped by the `moving` guard, which is the other half of "something weird": the button looked dead. The click is now queued and runs when the slide lands, ignoring a request that targets the step you're already on.

**[VaultLayout.tsx](src/layouts/VaultLayout.tsx)** — reaching `/signup` by browser history or a plain link left the vault at the hero anchor (61.8), i.e. the card sitting on top of the wheel. A non-animated arrival now snaps the anchor to 76.4.

