![Overview at 1440x900](docs/dashboard/1440-populated.png)

**Routes.** `/dashboard` (greeting + KPIs over the decision queue and the ledger), `/dashboard/vaults` (the same list, one column), `/dashboard/ledger` (the same grid full width with Status, Duration and a filter), `/dashboard/payments` and `/dashboard/settings` (heading only). One shell owns the rail, the strip and the data read, so moving between them does not remount anything.

**What the demo does.** Authorize moves a vault to held and raises `PAYMENT.AUTHORIZED`; approving costs a 1.618s hold that fires capture + unlock and says *"Payment captured. Files unlocked."*; releasing early drains the ring and does nothing; voiding dims the card and writes `PAYMENT.VOIDED`. Cards re-sort with a FLIP, KPIs count to their new values, and `Shift+D` opens a dev panel that fires any webhook by hand.

