<h3>1.3 State management</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Mock backend (server state):</strong> <code>src/lib/api.ts</code> keeps <code>vaults</code>, <code>events</code>,
  <code>checkedAt</code> and <code>questionsUsed</code> as module-level variables. Every call is an async function
  wrapped in <code>call()</code>, which adds latency and a 5% random failure. A pub/sub set (<code>listeners</code>)
  pushes ledger events to subscribers.</li>
  <li><strong>Global store (<code>src/lib/store.tsx</code>):</strong> a React context provider (<code>StoreProvider</code>,
  mounted in <code>src/main.tsx</code>) holds the vault and ledger view models and drives a timed replay of the payment
  lifecycle for the demo. It exposes <code>createVault</code>, <code>patch</code>, <code>approve</code>, and
  <code>startReplay</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Auth (<code>src/lib/mockAuth.ts</code>):</strong> a fake sign-in. <code>roleFor(email)</code> assigns a role
  from the address. The session is written to <code>sessionStorage</code>. Nothing is verified against a server.</li>
  <li><strong>Component state:</strong> local <code>useState</code> and <code>useEffect</code> in pages and panels. There
  is no Redux, Zustand or TanStack Query.</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.4 Main UI components</h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>src/layouts/VaultLayout.tsx</code>: the shared layout and landing visual sequence.</li>
