<h3>3.3 Notes on the contracts</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Vault status moves in one direction: awaiting_payment, held, audited, unlocked. A vault can also go to voided from audited or held.</li>
  <li><code>VaultCheck.state</code> is <code>queued</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>pass</code>, <code>warn</code> or <code>fail</code>. <code>source</code> is one of TEST LOG, BROWSER TEST, PIXEL SCAN or HTTP PROBE.</li>
  <li><code>SourceChip</code> also includes <code>DEMO CACHE</code>, which only marks an answer as cached. Real answers should set <code>cached</code> from the model response instead.</li>
  <li>Every write must check the same status rules the mock enforces (<code>expectStatus</code> in api.ts), and emit the matching ledger event in the same transaction.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Backend decisions for the team</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Hosting shape.</strong> Either add API routes to a Next.js app (the route handlers above map directly), or keep the Vite SPA and run a separate Node or Edge API. The contracts in section 3 are the same either way.</li>
  <li><strong>Payments.</strong> Authorize, capture and void map to PayPal order calls. Store <code>paypalOrderId</code> on the vault. The mock IDs are placeholders.</li>
  <li><strong>Auth.</strong> Replace <code>mockAuth.ts</code> with a real session. The role must come from the server, not from the email text.</li>
  <li><strong>Audit runner and AI.</strong> The check runner and the chat need real services. <code>checks:run</code> should stream per-check progress. The chat should call a model and report whether the answer came from cache.</li>
  <li><strong>Realtime.</strong> Replace the in-memory listener set with SSE (<code>/v1/events</code>) backed by the ledger table.</li>
</ol>

