The headline now lands at its final size on the very first painted frame — no reflow after paint.

## What was still wrong

The last measurable defect on the branch was a single 4.2px line-box shift in the headline at 1440 (including the t=715ms animation frames). Cause: `--vault-left` (which sets `--h1-max`, the headline's size) was only written once `f_001.webp` had **decoded**, so the headline was first laid out at the 68px fallback and then re-fitted to 46.9px one frame later. The frame is 16:9, so that number was knowable before the image existed.

## The change

- [HeroVault.tsx](src/components/HeroVault.tsx) — pulled the desktop rect math (cover-fit, 1.12 width cap, wheel pin) into one `desktopRect()` used by both paths, and added a `useLayoutEffect` that computes it from the frame's own 1920×1080 aspect and writes `--vault-left` in the same layout pass as the first paint. `paint()` then corrects it with the real image dimensions, which are identical.
- No colour, copy, timeline, vault, or button change.

