## 1. The half-loaded line

The cause was the headline's reveal, not loading. Each line was wiped in behind `clip-path: inset(0 0 100% 0) → inset(0 0 0 0)` while it rose 34px, so for the whole 0.618s tween every glyph was cut horizontally at the mask edge — you were seeing the top half of the letters. Because the lines are staggered (0.618 / 0.854 / 1.090s), the third line's sliced state was the last thing on screen, which read as "half of 'fairly.' arriving late".

- Each line now rises and fades with **no mask** — the glyphs are whole at every frame. Timings are untouched: line 1 at 0.618, line 2 at 0.854, line 3 at 1.090, all 0.618s, last line landing at **1.708s** — inside the 2.618s idle gate, as before.
- Measured over the full entrance at 1440 and 1920: **0 frames** where any line carried a clip. At line 3 opacity 0.65 the word "fairly." is fully formed, only dimmer.
- The dead `padding-bottom: 0.15em / margin-bottom: -0.15em` on `.h1-line` (which existed only to keep the mask off descenders) is gone; it was net-zero on layout, and the 21px headline-to-paragraph gap still measures 21px.

I also closed the other first-load hole I found while tracing: the start pose was applied only when the timeline was built (`ready && booted`), so there was a window where the entry gate had lifted but the copy was still painted at its *finished* state, then hidden and replayed. The pose is now applied in a layout effect as soon as the copy exists ([Hero.tsx](src/components/Hero.tsx), `armHeroIntro` in [hero-timeline.ts](src/components/hero-timeline.ts)). First visible frame on a cold load is now line 1 at 0.26–0.33 opacity with lines 2 and 3 still at 0 — never the finished headline.

## 2. The paragraph

[src/components/HeroCopy.tsx](src/components/HeroCopy.tsx) carries the full text again:

> VaultLance AI is an escrow platform for digital deliverables. Freelancers upload code and design files; clients test them live via AI analysis. Files unlock only after PayPal payment is captured, protecting both sides from non-payment and incomplete work.

## Checks

- `npx tsc --noEmit` → 0, `npm run build` → 0.
- Headline → paragraph gap 21px and paragraph → buttons gap 34px at every width; no wrapped headline line at 360 and up; no horizontal overflow at 1920/1440/1280/1024/390/360.
- CLS 0.0003 at 1440×900, 0.00013 at 1920×1080.
- Reduced motion: three lines and the paragraph at opacity 1 with no clip — final state, no entrance.
