The connector is back on the sign-in page.

## What broke it

My earlier fix for the landing made the connector line off-by-default: the svg carries `opacity: 0` and only `data-on="1"` reveals it, and that attribute was set exclusively by the hero's Sign in button (hover/focus). So on `/signin` the form did hand over the password field and the path *was* traced — `d` was set and the dash offset was 0 — but nothing ever set `data-on`, so the whole svg sat at opacity 0. The line was drawn, just invisible.

## The fix

In [HeroVault.tsx](src/components/HeroVault.tsx):

- Drawing from a form field now turns the line on (`holdConnector()` sets `data-on="1"` at 1024px and up). The off-at-rest rule stays exactly where it belongs — the hero's Sign in control.
- The mount-time reset no longer clears a line a form has already requested, which previously could race the sign-in page's first trace.
- `connectorFrom(null)` — leaving the form — drops `data-on` and the path, so the landing still starts with the line gone.

## Verified

At 1920, 1440 and 1024 on `/signin`: `data-on="1"`, computed opacity `1`, path present with `strokeDashoffset: 0`, running from the password field's right edge to the keypad. The crop above shows the teal dashed line intact between the field and the keypad.

Still holds after 4s (past the 1.4s trace loop) and across resizes to 1920 and 1280; a screenshot of that page matches the line you expected.

On the landing, unchanged: at rest `data-on="0"`, opacity 0, no path; hovering Sign in or tabbing to it gives `data-on="1"`, opacity 1, path drawn; leaving hides it again; navigating back from `/signin` leaves no line behind. `npx tsc --noEmit` → 0, `npm run build` → 0. Commit `ff9572d`, working tree clean, nothing pushed.
